  detector pkt_cdb_case      an over-reaching guard   dispatch count 1 -> 0
  (ACCEPT, already shipped)  that refuses in CMDOUT
  detector, 14 rows          mutA1                    MEASURED: base 0 -> mutA1 14

VACUOUS-BY-CONSTRUCTION CHECK: every row above names a channel that CAN vary under its
named mutant.

*** AND THE CHANNEL LINE'S OWN CLAIM, CHECKED A SECOND TIME. ***  Last round it held.
Here it holds again and pays more: **it is knowable at writing time that the shipped
detector cannot kill mutA2 or mutA3**, because their named channel is the post-re-arm
readback and no shipped row reads it -- which is the same fact as the floor finding,
reached from the row side instead of from the table side.  The two agree, which is the
first time this block has had an independent cross-check on its own conclusion.

